WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.401 --> 00:00:05.637
Projects lists everything your organization works on, in the order your agents serve it.

2
00:00:06.341 --> 00:00:08.651
Open Projects in the sidebar.

3
00:00:09.351 --> 00:00:18.242
New project asks for a name, a short key that card references start with, and a workflow. Code builds features from repositories.

4
00:00:18.946 --> 00:00:28.766
The project at the top is served first: agents take the next card from the highest project that has work. Drag a project, or use its arrows, to move it up.

5
00:00:29.470 --> 00:00:34.716
The gear opens the project settings. The chips at the top jump straight to a section.

6
00:00:35.416 --> 00:00:43.692
Under Repos, add the repository the agents work in: its address and a name. The DevOps engineer then clones it onto your computers.

7
00:00:45.911 --> 00:00:53.514
Set a monthly budget. At eighty percent you are warned, and at the limit nothing new starts until you raise it or override it for the month.

8
00:00:54.213 --> 00:01:04.950
Under Team, invite someone who has a Guildwise account by email, with Send invitation. They show as pending until they accept, and then help manage this project.

9
00:01:05.651 --> 00:01:11.303
Back on Projects, the new project has its place in the order. That is Projects.
